<LegalPage title="Submission Policy" updated="October 3, 2026" intro="How we treat the testimonies, questions, prayer requests and other messages you share with us.">
  <p>Thank you for trusting us with your story. This policy covers anything you send through the site, including Share Your Testimony, questions for John, podcast guest requests, responses to posts, and prayer requests.</p>

  <h2>You choose whether it's shared</h2>
  <p>Every form asks whether we may share what you send: with your first name, anonymously, or not at all. We follow your choice. <strong>Prayer requests are always private</strong> and are never published.</p>

  <h2>What you allow us to do</h2>
  <p>If you choose to let us share your submission, you give There You Are Jesus LLC a free, non-exclusive, worldwide permission to publish it on the site, in the podcast, in emails, and on our social media, and to lightly edit it for length, clarity and privacy (for example removing last names or locations). We won't change its meaning. You keep ownership of your story and can share it anywhere else.</p>
  <p>For anything beyond that, such as a book or film, we'll ask you first.</p>

  <h2>Changing your mind</h2>
  <p>You can ask us to remove a shared submission at any time by emailing <a href="mailto:john@thereyouarejesus.com">john@thereyouarejesus.com</a>. We'll take it down from the site and stop using it going forward; we can't recall emails already sent or episodes others have downloaded.</p>

  <h2>What you promise</h2>
  <p>Please only send stories that are yours to tell and true to the best of your knowledge. Don't include other people's private details without their permission, or anything unlawful, hateful or harassing. We may decline to publish any submission.</p>

  <h2>Ideas and suggestions</h2>
  <p>If you send ideas for the site, the podcast or products, we may use them without owing you anything, and we can't keep unsolicited ideas confidential.</p>

  <h2>If you or someone else is in danger</h2>
  <p>Our forms aren't monitored around the clock and can't respond to emergencies. If you or someone you know is in immediate danger, call 911 (in the U.S.) or your local emergency number. If you're struggling or thinking about suicide, call or text 988 to reach the 988 Suicide &amp; Crisis Lifeline in the U.S. If a child is being harmed, call the Childhelp National Child Abuse Hotline at 1-800-422-4453 or contact local authorities.</p>

  <h2>Questions</h2>
  <p>Email <a href="mailto:john@thereyouarejesus.com">john@thereyouarejesus.com</a>. How we store and protect submissions is described in our <a href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a>.</p>
</LegalPage>
